$Module harden 3 "TLS certificate match for SNI; optional client drop"

DESCRIPTION
===========

With multiple TLS certificates, Varnish may fall back to the **last**
one when SNI does not match—so the wrong site can get the wrong cert.
``harden`` stops that: the handshake only succeeds if the certificate
matches the client's SNI (hostname or IP). No SNI or no cert also stops
the handshake.

``harden.close()`` (client context only) drops the client connection
without an HTTP response (like nginx ``return 444``). It only fails the
transport; it does **not** end VCL handling or drop the VCL **busy** count.
If ``vcl_recv`` continues (e.g. into hash) after ``close()``, shutdown
can stall with ``shutdown waiting for N references on <name>`` until those
counts clear—so **always** follow with a terminal ``return``, e.g.
``return (synth(503, "Connection closed"));`` or ``return (fail);``.

$Event event
$Function VOID close()
$Restrict client

Close the client connection (no HTTP response). Must be followed immediately
by a terminal ``return`` (typically ``synth`` or ``fail`` in ``vcl_recv``).
